 font-size: 16px;">Good morning dear reader,</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">For years, conte=
nt creation in India lived in the margins. It was something done after coll=
ege hours, between freelance gigs, quietly from a bedroom desk. Visible, po=
pular, but rarely taken seriously as work.</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">Last week&rsquo;=
s Union Budget changed the tone. By formally recognising the creative or or=
ange economy, and committing funding to animation, gaming, visual effects a=
nd digital storytelling, the government signalled that content creation is =
no longer just a side hustle.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">With 15,500 cont=
ent-creator labs planned in schools and colleges, and new institutional bac=
king for creative education, the government has placed a meaningful bet on =
creators as future workers.</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">The excitement i=
s understandable. Recognition alone can shift behaviour. Parents begin to l=
isten differently. Students imagine longer runways. Early creators already =
seeing returns expect momentum to build as policy support deepens.</span></=
p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">Yet the harder t=
est lies ahead. India&rsquo;s skilling problem does not spare the creative =
economy. Strong execution, capable trainers, and industry-aligned coursewor=
k can turn these labs into well-equipped spaces that genuinely build employ=
able skills. Industry participation and outcome-based training will decide =
whether this becomes a pipeline or a placeholder.</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">If done right, t=
he upside is large. Jobs emerge quickly, gig work expands, and India moves =
from low-cost production to high-quality creation.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">The Budget has o=
pened the door. What happens next will decide whether content creation rema=
ins a side hustle or becomes a credible, long-term career.</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;">Read the full st=
ory here =F0=9F=91=87</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"line-height: 24px;"><span style=3D"font-family: Geo=
rgia, 'Times New Roman', Courier, serif; font-size: 16px;"><strong>&nbsp;</=
